{"text": "# Finding the Sum of Decimal Digits of 13^10\n\n## Step 1: Calculate 13^10\n\nI'll compute this by building up from smaller powers:\n\n- 13^1 = 13\n- 13^2 = 169\n- 13^3 = 13 \u00d7 169 = 2,197\n- 13^4 = 13 \u00d7 2,197 = 28,561\n- 13^5 = 13 \u00d7 28,561 = 371,293\n- 13^6 = 13 \u00d7 371,293 = 4,826,809\n- 13^7 = 13 \u00d7 4,826,809 = 62,748,517\n- 13^8 = 13 \u00d7 62,748,517 = 815,730,721\n- 13^9 = 13 \u00d7 815,730,721 = 10,604,499,373\n- 13^10 = 13 \u00d7 10,604,499,373 = **137,858,491,849**\n\n## Step 2: Identify the Decimal Digits\n\nThe decimal digits of 137,858,491,849 are:\n1, 3, 7, 8, 5, 8, 4, 9, 1, 8, 4, 9\n\n## Step 3: Sum the Digits\n\nAdding step-by-step:\n- 1 + 3 = 4\n- 4 + 7 = 11\n- 11 + 8 = 19\n- 19 + 5 = 24\n- 24 + 8 = 32\n- 32 + 4 = 36\n- 36 + 9 = 45\n- 45 + 1 = 46\n- 46 + 8 = 54\n- 54 + 4 = 58\n- 58 + 9 = **67**\n\n## Final Answer\n\n**67**", "usage": {"calls": 1, "input_tokens": 903, "output_tokens": 1518, "cost_usd": 0.008493, "latency_s": 12.88223385810852}, "model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "stop_reason": "end_turn"}